yne","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Perin Davey","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10947","person_slug":"perin-davey","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ross Cadell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_11004","person_slug":"ross-cadell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Health Legislation Amendment (Removal of Requirement for a Collaborative Arrangement) Bill 2024 - Second Reading - Medicare benefits for services rendered to prisoners","noes":35,"question":"The majority voted against [amendments](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2024-05-16.254.3) moved by NSW Senator [David Shoebridge](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/david_shoebridge) (NSW), which means it failed. ### Amendment text > *That the House of Representatives be requested to make the following amendments:* > > *(1) Clause 1, page 1 (line 6), after \"Arrangement\", insert \"and Other Measures\".* > > *(2) Clause 2, page 2 (at the end of the table), add:* > >> *3. Schedule 2* >> >> *The day after this Act receives the Royal Assent.* > > *(3) Schedule 1, heading, page 3 (line 1), omit \"Amendments\", substitute \"Removal of Requirement for a Collaborative Arrangement\".* > > *(4) Page 3 (after line 29), at the end of the Bill, add:* > >> *Schedule 2 — Medicare benefits for services rendered to prisoners* >> >> *Health Insurance Act 1973* >> >> *1 Subsection 8(1A)* >> >>> *Insert:* >>> >>>> *in gaol: see subsection (1B).* >> >> *2 After subsection 8(1A)* >> >>> *Insert:* >>> >>>> *(1B) For the purposes of this Part, a person is in gaol if:* >>>> >>>>> *(a) the person is being lawfully detained (in prison or elsewhere) while under sentence for conviction of an offence and not on release on parole or licence; or* >>>>> >>>>> *(b) the person is undergoing a period of custody pending trial or sentencing for an offence.* >> >> *3 After subsection 19(2)* >> >>> *Insert:* >>> >>>> *(2A) Subsection (2) does not apply in relation to a professional service that has been rendered to a person if the person was in gaol at the time the service was rendered.* > *Statement pursuant to the order of the Senate of 26 June 2000* > > *Amendment (4)* > >> *Amendment (4) amends the Health Insurance Act 1973 to provide for Medicare benefits to be payable in respect of professional services rendered to persons in gaol. It is framed as a request because its effect will be to increase the scope of professional services in respect of which Medicare benefits are payable, ","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-8935","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-05-16/42"}
